# daimon

Loopback CLI at `http://127.0.0.1:{{api_port}}`. Compact JSON on stdout, errors as compact JSON on stderr (exit 1; `daimon wait` timeout exits 2). Daemon auto-spawns on first call (set `DAIMON_NO_SPAWN=1` to skip).

## Verbs

- `daimon overview` → workspace snapshot (totals, needs-attention, recently-changed). **Start here.**
- `daimon context <name> [--budget <chars>]` → the whole picture for ONE app in one call: status/framework, top error groups, last crash, last test run + failures, compile stats, suspect commits, locks. **Call this first when debugging an app**, then make targeted calls. `--budget` drops sections lowest-priority-first (listed in `truncated[]`).
- `daimon test <name> [--timeout <dur>]` → run the project's own test suite once (vitest/jest/pytest/go/cargo/dotnet, or `overrides.<name>.testCommand`). Parsed failures `{suite,test,file,line,message}` + totals; exit 0 pass / 1 failures / 2 timeout / 5 locked by another agent (`--steal` overrides). `daimon test-history <name> [--flaky]` → recent runs / flaky tests.
- `daimon search <query> [--app <a>] [--since 24h] [--kind logs|errors|events]` → full-text search over everything daimon has seen (log lines, errors, events). Hits are `{kind,app,ts,snippet,ref}`; trailing `*` = prefix search.
- `daimon list` → `{name,status,port,health,errCount,lastChangeMs}` per app. `--full` for v0.4 form.
- `daimon status <name>` → compact `{name,status,port,url,health,errCount,lastChangeMs,uptime}`. `--full` for events/metrics.
- `daimon ensure <name> [--until serving|healthy] [--timeout 180]` → one call: starts if stopped, blocks to target, returns terminal state.
- `daimon ensure-up <profile>` → same for an entire profile; cascades dependencies.
- `daimon errors <name> [--since 5m|--since-last --client claude] [--structured]` → dedup'd errors, compact `{file,line,col,code,message}`. `daimon errors --group` (no name) → all apps' errors grouped by stack fingerprint.
- `daimon frameworks` → the framework adapter registry: built-in + custom profiles, which apps each matched, rejection stats.
- `daimon logs <name> [--tail N] [--since 30s]` → recent log lines.
- `daimon start|stop|restart <name>` · `daimon up|down [<profile>]` · `daimon wait <name> --until healthy --timeout 60s`.
- `daimon why <name>` → one-shot forensics: status, last crash (exit code + final log lines), grouped 24h errors, regressions, restart-storm state, env changes since last healthy, suspect commit, doctor findings. `daimon why-empty` → explain an empty `list`.
- `daimon report [--since 24h|7d] [--app <a>] [--workspace <l>] [--md]` → the digest: per-app uptime %, error groups (new/recurring/resolved), test pass-rate + flakiest, compile p50/p95 + regressions, crashes/storms, agent activity, env changes. `--md` for human/Slack-ready markdown.
- `daimon env <name>` → convention env files (found/missing) + key NAMES from the last spawn snapshot; `daimon env diff <name>` → files/keys added/removed/changed between spawns. Values are NEVER shown — open the file itself.
- `daimon ports` → app → port → source (`pinned|pool|announced`) → pid, plus foreign holders of pool/pinned ports. Pool auto-assignment via `ports.pool` config; only frameworks whose registry row documents `portFlag`/`portEnv` participate.
- `daimon mute <name> [--for 2h]` / `daimon unmute <name>` → silence OS notifications per app (events/webhooks unaffected); shown in status.
- `daimon doctor [--auto-fix] [--dry-run] [--self]` → config + env sanity check; `--auto-fix` repairs orphan daemon, stale lock, missing search root, corrupt history DB, and kills a VERIFIED orphan daimon holding the api port (signature-checked; non-daimon holders are never killed); `--self` runs daimon's own heap / event-loop-lag / history-db query checks.
- `daimon self` → daimon's own runtime metrics (pid, version, uptime, rss, heap, event-loop lag, history-db p95). Useful in bug reports.
- `daimon plugin list|show <name>|validate <path>` → manage doctor plug-ins. Plug-ins live at `~/.daimon/plugins/doctor-*.mjs` and are inert until their `name` is added to `doctor.autoFix.permitted` — the same opt-in gate built-in rules use. If a plug-in is enabled in this workspace it will appear in `daimon plugin list` with `status:"ok"` and a `findings` array.
- `daimon completion <bash|zsh|fish|powershell>` → emit shell-completion script. Verbs and (when the daemon is up) app names autocomplete.

## Patterns

- **First call in a session:** `daimon overview`. If `totals.apps === 0`, the response includes `_meta.suggestion` — follow it.
- **Debugging one app:** `daimon context <name>` first (one call replaces status+errors+logs+history), then targeted calls for whatever it surfaces.
- **App keeps dying:** `daimon why <name>` — the last crash's exit code and final log lines are already there; don't tail logs hoping to catch it.
- **After editing code:** `daimon test <name>`, then `daimon errors <name> --since-last --client claude` for compile errors.
- **"Where did I see that string?":** `daimon search "<needle>" --since 24h`.
- **"What happened today/this week?":** `daimon report --since 24h` (add `--md` when pasting to a human).
- **"It worked yesterday":** `daimon env diff <name>` — an env-file change is the culprit half the time; `daimon why <name>` includes the same hint as `envChanged`.
- **Bring up one app idempotently:** `daimon ensure <name>`. Replaces the old `status → start → wait → status` sequence.
- **Diff-style error checks:** `daimon errors <name> --since-last --client claude` returns only what's new since the last call.

## Do not

- Do not run `nx serve`, `ng serve`, or `npm start` directly — go through `daimon ensure`.
- Do not parse log files; `daimon errors` is already dedup'd and parsed.
- Do not retry blindly on `daimon wait` timeout (exit 2) — read `daimon errors` and `daimon why` first.
- Do not bind non-loopback ports. Do not modify user source files via daimon.
